 Experiment 42: To Automate Checkbox and Radio Button Selection Using Selenium WebDriver

AIM
To write a Selenium WebDriver program to automate checkbox and radio button selection on a web page.

ALGORITHM
1. Start the program.
2. Launch the Chrome browser using Selenium WebDriver.
3. Open the practice web page.
4. Locate the checkbox and select it.
5. Locate the radio button and select it.
6. Verify whether both are selected.
7. Close the browser.

CODE

**File name: `CheckboxRadioTest.java`**

```java
import org.openqa.selenium.By;
import org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;
import org.openqa.selenium.WebElement;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

public class CheckboxRadioTest {

    @Test
    public void selectCheckboxAndRadioButton() {

        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        driver.get("https://demoqa.com/checkbox");

        driver.manage().window().maximize();

        WebElement checkbox = driver.findElement(
            By.xpath("//button[@title='Toggle']")
        );

        checkbox.click();

        WebElement radioPage = driver.findElement(
            By.xpath("//span[text()='Radio Button']")
        );

        radioPage.click();

        WebElement radioButton = driver.findElement(
            By.xpath("//label[@for='yesRadio']")
        );

        radioButton.click();

        WebElement selectedRadio = driver.findElement(
            By.id("yesRadio")
        );

        assertTrue(selectedRadio.isSelected());

        System.out.println("Checkbox and radio button selection completed.");

        driver.quit();
    }
}
```

## INPUT
- Website: https://demoqa.com/checkbox
- Checkbox: Home
- Radio Button: Yes

## EXPECTED OUTPUT

```text
Checkbox selected successfully.
Radio button selected successfully.
Checkbox and radio button selection completed.
```

## RESULT
Thus, checkbox and radio button selection was automated successfully using Selenium WebDriver.
